    <!-- ═══════════ WORK / PLATES ═══════════ -->
    <section class="sec" id="work">
      <aside class="note" aria-hidden="true"><span>Plate set 01–03</span></aside>
      <div class="body">
        <h2>Work <span class="h2km" lang="km">គម្រោង</span></h2>

        <article class="plate">
          <div class="plate-head">
            <span class="pno">Plate 01</span>
            <span class="ptitle">Provida SFA: offline-first sales platform</span>
            <span class="pdate">2025</span>
          </div>
          <div class="plate-body">
            <p>
              Sales reps in the field order without signal. Orders queue on-device with idempotency
              keys and sync safely when the network returns, with no duplicates and no lost work. The app
              tracks customer visits and stock counts, and closes the day with reports: sales
              history with order-status breakdowns, end-of-day summaries, and activity maps.
            </p>
            <p class="tech">Next.js (PWA) · TypeScript · Tailwind CSS · IndexedDB sync queue</p>
            <pre class="code"><code>// Concept — a stable idempotency key rides with every queued order,
// so a retry after a flaky network can never create a duplicate.
queue.enqueue('order.create', order.withIdempotencyKey());</code></pre>
            <p class="redact">Pattern shown conceptually — production internals redacted.</p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="plate">
          <div class="plate-head">
            <span class="pno">Plate 02</span>
            <span class="ptitle">Provida Report Platform: Laravel order backend</span>
            <span class="pdate">2025</span>
          </div>
          <div class="plate-body">
            <p>
              The API behind the SFA app: order approval workflow with Sage ERP sync, per-customer
              sales dashboards, and mobile endpoints scoped by sales rep, on MySQL with
              JSON-scoped territories.
            </p>
            <p class="tech">Laravel · MySQL · Vue 3 · Redis</p>
            <pre class="code"><code>-- Concept — per-status counts in a single pass over today's orders
SUM(CASE WHEN status = 'pending' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS pending_count</code></pre>
            <p class="redact">Pattern shown conceptually — production schema redacted.</p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="plate">
          <div class="plate-head">
            <span class="pno">Plate 03</span>
            <span class="ptitle">TOTP Shield: self-hosted 2FA as a service</span>
            <span class="pdate">2025</span>
          </div>
          <div class="plate-body">
            <p>
              A central two-factor authentication provider that other applications integrate with
              through a REST API. Client apps enrol users via QR code, verify OTPs at login, and
              delegate all TOTP handling to the service. The web dashboard manages API apps,
              monitors usage, and administers users across three roles.
            </p>
            <p class="tech">Ruby on Rails 7.1 · MariaDB · Devise + devise-two-factor · ROTP · Docker</p>
            <pre class="code"><code># Concept — relying apps delegate all TOTP handling over a keyed API
POST /setup   → enrol user, return QR + secret
POST /verify  → check OTP at every login</code></pre>
            <p class="redact">Pattern shown conceptually — production endpoints redacted.</p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <h3 class="loghead">Field log — additional work</h3>
        <ol class="log">
          <li>
            <span class="lno">L.01</span>
            <div>
              <h4>Database as a Service</h4>
